At 17:48 19.06.2005, you wrote:
>Hi all, i'm here again,
>
>my question is, how can i pass a boot-parameter to the sarge installation-cd
>(netinst-iso)? Everyone talks about the Boot-Prompt, but i get no prompt.
>The installer runs always through, and let me pass no parameters to the
>kernel (expert, snd-ad1848 <params>, ad1848 <params>, etc.) What goes wrong
>here? Is there a boot-prompt only at the i386-installation? When i try to pass
>the parameters with aboot from srm-console i get only different kernel-panics
>(even when i try the parameters from aboot.conf). Please help.

it seems that you have BOOT_OSFLAGS in SRM set. This are the default 
parameters added to the commandline of the "boot" command. If it contains 
"0" it is the same like starting "boot dka... -fl 0" which starts the first 
config item in aboot.conf on the CD.

Clear your BOOT_OSFLAGS variable first!
then type "boot dka..." and nothing else. You will then get a aboot prompt.

