I am not sure that this works. Can you try explicitly specifying the
entire command, i.e.,
b 2/vmlinuz ro root=3D/dev/hda2 initrd=3D/initrd.img ad1848 ispnp=3D0 io=3D=
530 irq=3D9 dma=3D0 dma2=3D1
(replace the first part with your actual  contents of the 0th entry).

Easier yet, add an entry into etc/aboot.conf with the full command
before rebooting, then you can simply type, e.g., "9" for the test
case.

